<a href="/settings">← Settings</a><header class="page-header asset-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">DATABASE + DOCUMENT FILES</p><h1>A private copy you can take with you.</h1><p class="muted">Export an encrypted backup, protected by a passphrase you choose.</p></div></header>
<?php require ROOT.'/app/Core/views/notices.php'; ?>
<div class="two-col"><section class="card"><h2>Create an encrypted backup</h2><p class="muted">Includes a consistent SQLite snapshot and all uploaded documents, including Trash. AES-256-GCM authenticates every chunk. The passphrase is used for this backup and is not saved.</p><form method="post" action="/settings/encrypted/export" hx-boost="false" class="stack"><?= csrf_field() ?><label>Backup passphrase<input type="password" name="passphrase" minlength="12" maxlength="1024" autocomplete="new-password" required></label><label>Confirm passphrase<input type="password" name="passphrase_confirm" minlength="12" maxlength="1024" autocomplete="new-password" required></label><p class="footnote">Use at least 12 characters. Keep this passphrase somewhere you can recover it: LifeOS cannot reset an encrypted backup’s passphrase. This protects the exported file; the live database and local document files remain unencrypted.</p><button>Export encrypted backup</button></form></section>
<section class="card"><h2>Restore an encrypted backup</h2><p class="muted">Replaces both the database and uploaded files. The full archive is checked before current data changes. LifeOS keeps a complete local safety copy of your previous database and documents.</p><form method="post" action="/settings/encrypted/restore" enctype="multipart/form-data" hx-boost="false" class="stack" data-confirm="Replace the current database and all uploaded document files with this backup?"><?= csrf_field() ?><label>Encrypted backup<input name="backup" type="file" accept=".lifeosbk" required></label><label>Backup passphrase<input name="passphrase" type="password" minlength="12" maxlength="1024" autocomplete="off" required></label><label>Type RESTORE to confirm<input name="confirm" pattern="RESTORE" autocomplete="off" required></label><button class="danger">Restore database & documents</button></form><p class="footnote">Backups must match the installed module/migration set. Maximum encrypted file: 256 MiB. Export supports archives up to 240 MiB compressed, 512 MiB expanded, and 5,000 uploaded files.</p></section></div>
<section class="card"><h2>Recent encrypted backups</h2><?php if (!$encryptedFiles): ?><div class="empty"><h3>No data yet.</h3><p>Create your first encrypted copy above.</p></div><?php else: ?><ul class="backup-list"><?php foreach ($encryptedFiles as $file): ?><li><a hx-boost="false" href="/settings/encrypted/download/<?= e(basename($file)) ?>"><?= e(basename($file)) ?></a><small><?= e(number_format(filesize($file)/1024/1024,2)) ?> MiB</small></li><?php endforeach; ?></ul><?php endif; ?></section>
<?php if ($safetyFolders): ?><section class="card"><h2>Previous data kept after restores</h2><p class="muted">Each folder below contains the previous database.db and uploads directory. These safety copies are local and unencrypted. Keep them until you have checked the restored data.</p><ul class="backup-list"><?php foreach ($safetyFolders as $folder): ?><li>data/backups/<?= e(basename($folder)) ?></li><?php endforeach; ?></ul></section><?php endif; ?>
